Guard the runDiskCheck call for builds without -DKNULLI

ApiSystem::runDiskCheck is declared and defined under #ifdef KNULLI, but
ThreadedDiskCheck.cpp calls it unconditionally -- the KNULLI CI always
builds with -DKNULLI=ON, so upstream never sees the standalone build
break ("'class ApiSystem' has no member named 'runDiskCheck'"). RelicOS
M10 builds standalone on purpose (no /userdata path hardcoding); with
the guard the disk-check notification simply closes immediately, which
is fine: the feature drives a knulli-disk-check script that does not
exist on this rootfs anyway.

--- a/es-app/src/guis/knulli/ThreadedDiskCheck.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/guis/knulli/ThreadedDiskCheck.cpp
@@ -38,10 +38,12 @@
 
 void ThreadedDiskCheck::run()
 {
+#ifdef KNULLI
 	ApiSystem::getInstance()->runDiskCheck([this](const std::string info)
 	{
 		updateNotificationComponentContent(info);
 	});
+#endif
 
 	delete this;
 	ThreadedDiskCheck::mInstance = nullptr;
